@cofyc extenders.Filter() can set the status of failed node as `UnschedulableAndUnresolvable`, then we should be fix the logic:

https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/b339ed0e75c5815d49c5c4d118d4b9858b4babc4/pkg/scheduler/core/generic_scheduler.go#L509-L515

to respect the `UnschedulableAndUnresolvable` status returned by extenders.Filter().

Add an implicit contract with extenders may change the meaning of the failed msg. How about adding a new field?

The new field can be a map to supersede `FailedNodes`. I agree we should not depend on internal status constants in the framework, we can use string as the status value, e.g. `Unschedulable`, `UnschedulableAndUnresolvable`.

Or the new field can be a map which includes `UnschedulableAndUnresolvable` nodes, e.g.

```
type ExtenderFilterResult struct { 
    // ...
 	// Filtered out nodes where the pod can't be scheduled and the failure messages 
 	FailedNodes FailedNodesMap 
 	// Filtered out nodes where the pod can't be scheduled and the failure messages
    // Failed nodes in this map are unresolvable and will be skipped in the preemption phase.
 	FailedAndUnresolvableNodes FailedNodesMap 
 } 
```

I guess 2) is not possible because it adds an extra deps to `k/k` as you said. I'm ok with option 1) and 3).

@resouer @ahg-g @alculquicondor what do you think?

If you agree, I can send a PR to implement it. This gives extender the ability to mark nodes unscheduable and unresolvable then nodes can be skipped in the preempt phase.
